<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Quinn to offer EU summit new EMU pact compromise.</title>
<headline>Quinn to offer EU summit new EMU pact compromise.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Finance Minister Ruairi Quinn will present a revised compromise proposal for an EMU stability pact to EU leaders and fellow finance ministers when they reconvene at 1500 GMT after lunch at a summit meeting, an EU diplomat said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said the proposal was close to what finance ministers had drafted at a marathon overnight meeting but had been refined after Quinn met a number of key finance ministers on Friday morning.</p>
<p>The diplomat would not be drawn on whether Germany and France had accepted the new proposal. He said the situation was &quot;fragile&quot;.</p>
</text>
